@startuml
layout compact
package services::opc::model {
  abstract class TripItem {
    + {abstract} price()
    + {abstract} supplier_kind()
    + {abstract} cancellation_deadline(festival_start)
  }
  class FestivalPass {
    + price()
    + supplier_kind()
    + cancellation_deadline(festival_start)
  }
  class LodgingStay {
    + price()
    + supplier_kind()
    + cancellation_deadline(festival_start)
  }
  class Experience {
    + price()
    + supplier_kind()
    + cancellation_deadline(festival_start)
  }
  abstract class TransportItem {
    + cancellation_deadline(festival_start)
  }
  class ShuttleRide {
    + price()
    + supplier_kind()
  }
}
FestivalPass --|> TripItem
LodgingStay --|> TripItem
Experience --|> TripItem
TransportItem --|> TripItem
ShuttleRide --|> TransportItem
package services::opc::payloads
package services::website::checkout
services::opc::payloads ..> services::opc::model : «import»
services::website::checkout ..> services::opc::payloads : «use»
note right of TripItem
TripItem declares its three operations
abstract (services/opc/model/items.py:17).
TransportItem defines only
cancellation_deadline
(services/opc/model/items.py:92).
end note
note left of TripItem
Key: UML 2.5.1 class diagram.
Hollow triangle: generalization.
Italic: abstract class or operation.
Each class lists the operations it
defines itself.
end note
note left of services::opc::payloads
Folder with its name inside: a Python
module, shown without its contents.
Dashed arrow «import»: the module
imports from the package at its head.
ITEM_TYPES lists the item classes
that an order may name: FestivalPass,
LodgingStay, ShuttleRide, Experience
(services/opc/payloads.py:15).
end note
note right of services::website::checkout
Dashed arrow «use»: the module depends
on the other without importing it.
_item writes each item's type as text,
such as "ShuttleRide"
(services/website/checkout.py:89),
for payloads to read. The website
imports nothing from the OPC.
end note
@enduml
